 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nDate property values not updating correctly in core properties\n\nDescription\n\nIt seems there's an issue with updating date property values in the core properties. When attempting to change the `last_printed` date property, the expected XML output does not match the actual result. Here's a simple way to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nimport datetime as dt\nfrom docx.oxml.coreprops import CT_CoreProperties\nfrom docx.oxml import parse_xml\n\n# Create a core properties element\ncoreProperties = '<cp:coreProperties xmlns:cp=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/metadata/core-properties\" xmlns:dcterms=\"http://purl.org/dc/terms/\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"/>'\ncore_properties = CT_CoreProperties(parse_xml(coreProperties))\n\n# Set the last_printed property\ncore_properties.last_printed = dt.datetime(2014, 6, 4, 4)\n\n# Expected XML output\nexpected_xml = '<cp:coreProperties xmlns:cp=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/metadata/core-properties\" xmlns:dcterms=\"http://purl.org/dc/terms/\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"><cp:lastPrinted>2014-06-04T04:00:00Z</cp:lastPrinted></cp:coreProperties>'\n\n# Check if the XML matches the expected output\nassert core_properties.xml == expected_xml, \"The XML output does not match the expected result.\"\n```\n\nThe `last_printed` property should be updated to reflect the correct date and time in the expected format, but it seems to be failing to do so. This issue might be related to recent changes in the datetime handling logic. Reported by CodeCrafter.\n</issue>\n",
